    "turn_idx": 337,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and that's something that I think all of us, certainly in this environment with President Trump, people will say, well, if you oppose the President, if you're opposed to some of his policies and his behavior, it should be your role to oppose him on everything. I don't think that's a case. I think that people criticized Mitch McConnell for making that statement that our role is to make Barack Obama one-term president and to just try to hobble him in that regard. I will still vote with this president when I think he's right and oppose him when I think he's wrong. And I think that's my responsibility in the Senate.",
