      },
      {
        "text": "The current level of polarization in politics is concerning.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "This cycle of reciprocal obstruction has persisted since then.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "If procedural obstruction is used now, future Democrats will likely use similar tactics in response.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "During the Clarence Thomas and Judge Bork Supreme Court hearings in the late 80s and early 90s, no senator proposed a filibuster despite controversy.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Republicans reciprocated by using procedural tactics to block Democratic nominees after gaining power.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
