    "turn_text": "Yeah, but when you look at the big challenges we've had in the past, I mean we've gone through, all you have to do is go to the National Archives up in the legislative vault and view some of the relics and manuscripts and what not talking about what we've gone through as a country. We've gone through a civil war, a revolutionary war to start, dealt with issues like civil rights, women's suffrage, and we've always rose to the occasion, risen to the occasion. I think that some of the issues that we face on the fiscal side are really daunting. On the world stage, there are some real challenges there in terms of our role. You know, the biggest challenge we have is having a functioning legislative body and administration. If we have a functioning body here, we can deal with those big problems. And I do think in the end that voters will demand that. They'll want, again, not people who scream at each other, but people who will actually sit down and solve problems.",
